  "worked_solution": "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+t) \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}-6t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration when $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =8(1)^{3}-6(1)+1 \\\\  & =8-6+1 \\\\  & =3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
